Package: idmapaudit
Title: Audit the Sensitivity of Pathway Enrichment to Gene-ID-Mapping Choice
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Ethan", "Ye", email = "ethan.ye.201010@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Given a fixed differential expression result, idmapaudit varies
    only the gene-identifier-mapping strategy used to build the enrichment
    query list and background (Ensembl versioned/unversioned, Entrez via
    first-hit or list resolution, HGNC symbol via org.Hs.eg.db or biomaRt),
    reruns a standard ORA/GSEA enrichment battery across pathway databases
    (GO, KEGG, Reactome, WikiPathways) for every mapping branch, and reports
    a per-pathway fragility score that quantifies how much of the enrichment
    call depends on the mapping choice rather than the underlying biology.
    Includes a mapping-noise null model to separate structured mapping-driven
    instability from what finite-list-size sampling alone would produce.
